<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kousséri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1900</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kousséri was fought on 22 April 1900 near Kousséri, in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, between French forces under Commandant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amedee-francois-lamy">Amédée-François Lamy</a> and the army of the warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabih-az-zubayr">Rabih az-Zubayr</a>, ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a>. The French won, and both Lamy and Rabih were killed. The victory opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a> region to French conquest and led to the founding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndjamena">Fort-Lamy</a>, now N'Djamena.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kousseri.jpg" alt="Battle of Kousséri" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lou tresor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mort_du_Commandant_Lamy_2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
